Theorem RL-14a: cleanup obligations preserve exact logical identities

  Preconditions:
    - RL-14a consumes realized logical release and user-drop events.
    - CleanupObligation records event ids, drop-plan id, field order, normal
      exits, unwind exits, and logical lifetime-end events.
    - Physical cleanup encoding is a planner and adapter concern.

  Soundness property:
    Forall exact cleanup obligation C:

      (P1) Every release event in C is covered on each applicable normal exit.

      (P2) Every release event in C is covered on each applicable unwind exit.

      (P3) Event ids, drop-plan id, and ordered traversal are unchanged.

      (P4) Logical lifetime-end event ids are unchanged.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by checking exact membership and order. The
    negative direction rejects a missing unwind release or changed identity.

    Part (P1/P2/P3/P4) - cleanup grid:
      normal_exit_complete -> true
      unwind_exit_complete -> true
      logical_identity_preserved -> true
      lifetime_end_identity_preserved -> true
      Coverage gate: 4 cleanup cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl14a_cleanup_obligation;
        cleanupCoversNormalAndUnwind plus identity checks)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-14a by preserving exact CleanupObligation releases, drop plan, traversal order, normal/unwind coverage, and logical lifetime-end identity
